From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: make the net selftests module selectable and off by default

NET_SELFTESTS carries no prompt and is def_tristate PHYLIB, so it is built
as a module whenever phylib is (here pulled in by the DWC2 host USB-Ethernet
drivers); those drivers also imply it. Nothing loads it on a device - it is
a kselftest helper.

Give it a prompt so a board config can turn it off; phylib and its users are
unaffected.

--- a/net/Kconfig
+++ b/net/Kconfig
@@ -414,7 +414,7 @@
 	bool
 
 config NET_SELFTESTS
-	def_tristate PHYLIB
+	tristate "net selftests"
 	depends on PHYLIB && INET
 
 config NET_SOCK_MSG
